      "writtenOn": "2021-11-23T08:06:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think the name is more readable per se. There are two places where you\u0027ll see the name.\n❶ At definition site, i.e. here. Here, you could have it simply explained in comments.\n/* Initial version */\nVERSION_1\n/* Version 2 adds support for carrier template */\nVERSION_2\n\n❷ At use site. The problem with the use site is that you don\u0027t really know what comes after what. So you\u0027ll look at VERSION_SUPPORT_CARRIER_TEMPLATE and VERSION_SUPPORT_TRANSMOGRIUM and you won\u0027t know which came first.\n\nThat\u0027s why I thought 1 and 2 were better.\n\nNow maybe you can argue that at the use site, when you write the code you always write for the latest version, and when you read then you\u0027ll always see it in order in the code because previous versions are always supported. And you could add a comment about order at the use site.\n\nWith this in mind, if you prefer your current scheme I will not insist further, so up to you.",
